1
00:04:52,173 --> 00:04:58,173
The harder the life, the sweeter the song.

2
00:09:44,347 --> 00:09:50,347
Crazy Heart is a drama, music, romance film directed by Scott Cooper.

3
00:14:36,521 --> 00:14:42,521
When reporter Jean Craddock interviews Bad Blake—an alcoholic, seen-better-days country music legend—they connect,
and the hard-living crooner sees a possible saving grace in a life with Jean and her young son.

4
00:19:28,695 --> 00:19:34,695
Bad Blake, played by Jeff Bridges.

5
00:24:20,869 --> 00:24:26,869
Jean Craddock, played by Maggie Gyllenhaal.

6
00:29:13,043 --> 00:29:19,043
Wayne, played by Robert Duvall.

7
00:34:05,217 --> 00:34:11,217
Tommy Sweet, played by Colin Farrell.

8
00:38:57,391 --> 00:39:03,391
Bill Wilson, played by Tom Bower.

9
00:43:49,565 --> 00:43:55,565
Jack Greene, played by Paul Herman.

10
00:48:41,739 --> 00:48:47,739
Crazy Heart is a 2009 American drama film, written and directed
by Scott Cooper in his feature directorial debut.

11
00:53:33,913 --> 00:53:39,913
Based on the 1987 novel of the same name by Thomas Cobb, the
story was inspired by country singer Hank Thompson.

12
00:58:26,086 --> 00:58:32,086
Starring Jeff Bridges, Maggie Gyllenhaal, Colin Farrell, and Robert Duvall, the film follows an alcoholic country singer
and songwriter who tries to turn his life around after beginning a relationship with a young journalist.

13
01:03:18,260 --> 01:03:24,260
Bridges, Farrell, and Duvall also sing in the film.

14
01:08:10,434 --> 01:08:16,434
Filming took place in 2008 throughout New Mexico,
as well as Houston and Los Angeles.

15
01:13:02,608 --> 01:13:08,608
Original music for the film was composed by T Bone
Burnett, Stephen Bruton, and Ryan Bingham.

16
01:17:54,782 --> 01:18:00,782
It was dedicated to Bruton, who died the same year the film was made.

17
01:22:46,956 --> 01:22:52,956
The film was produced by Country Music Television and was originally acquired by Paramount Vantage for a
direct-to-video release, but was later purchased by Fox Searchlight Pictures for theatrical release.

18
01:27:39,130 --> 01:27:45,130
Crazy Heart opened in theaters in the United States on December 16, 2009.

19
01:32:31,304 --> 01:32:37,304
From its $7 million budget, it amassed domestic earnings of $39.5 million
plus $7.9 international for a worldwide total of $47.4 million.

20
01:37:23,478 --> 01:37:29,478
The film was met with critical acclaim and received three nominations at the 82nd Academy Awards, winning Best
Actor for Bridges and Best Original Song for "The Weary Kind", written by Bingham and Burnett.

21
01:42:15,652 --> 01:42:21,652
The film explores themes of journalist, taxi, country music, guitar, musician.

22
01:47:07,826 --> 01:47:13,826
The tone is uplifting and emotional and thought_provoking.
